# AsciiDoc math

Prefer Unicode over formal math: `ᵀ` `√` `₀₁₂₃` `⁰¹²³` `∑` `≠` `≤` `→` `∈`. Use dual-format guards only when Unicode cannot express the notation.

| Scope | `ifndef::env-github` (AsciiDoc) | `ifdef::env-github` (GitHub) |
|-------|---------------------------------|------------------------------|
| Inline | `\(...\)`, `stem:[...]` | `$...$` |
| Block | `[stem]++++...++++` | `` ```math ... ``` `` (preferred) or `$$...$$` |

- Prefer `[stem]++++` over `[latexmath]++++`. Prefer `` ```math `` over `$$` (fenced math is not rewritten by GitHub's Markdown preprocessor).
- Every math expression must sit in an `ifndef` / `ifdef` pair. Wrong syntax in the wrong guard, or math outside guards, is an error.
- Do not use `[source, math]`.
- In `ifdef`, `$...$` must not touch CJK: put a space between `$` and any adjacent Chinese character or punctuation.
- After editing math, run: `python tools/check-math-expression.py <file.asc>`
